# Inputs for the dashboard lock, `requirements-dashboard.txt`. Edit this file,
# never the lock; regenerate the lock with the command in its header.
#
# The dashboard runs `AgentPlatform` in-process (see `dashboard/app.py:
# get_platform()`), so it needs the whole platform plus Streamlit. The package
# set itself comes from pyproject extras; this file only adds two things:
#
# 1. The API lock as a constraint, so every package both runtimes share
#    resolves to the *same* version. Two deployments of one platform must not
#    skew.
# 2. The dashboard versions the pages were actually tested against. A resolve
#    left to itself picks the newest Streamlit, and an untested Streamlit is a
#    different product (`components.v1.html` is deprecated upstream).
#    pandas is not imported by the dashboard; it is pinned only because
#    Streamlit pulls it in and a lock must pin everything.

-c requirements-api.txt

streamlit==1.62.0
altair==6.2.2
pandas==3.0.5
